  "notes": "Two independent failure origins converge on the concurrent-inoperability consequence: the Division I CS Chiller trip (unrelated equipment failure, not separately cause-coded) and the Division II fan belt degradation (cause code E). Only the belt-wear/PM-interval chain is CAUSED_BY the coded cause; the chiller trip is modeled as a parallel FailureMode leading to the same shared consequence per rule 5, but has no CAUSED_BY edge since block 13 attributes cause E only to the VI/FAN component. No BACKED_UP_BY edges emitted since narrative states both trains were concurrently inoperable rather than one backing up the other. Docket 05000387 corresponds to Unit 1 per FORM-366 fields, though narrative covers both Units 1 and 2 conditions."
